WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.980
BETH: Many individuals with autism
are perfectly able and willing to

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:09.700
work, but only 21.7% are in full
or part-time employment, due to the

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.000
barriers they face in gaining employment.

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:16.689
JOE: Individuals with autism can offer
a wide range of skills and knowledge,

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:21.570
qualities and attributes to an employer,
however the field of employment is

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.400
a challenging and full of barriers
which many struggle to overcome.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.230
These barriers may be different
for each individual depending on

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.419
where they are on the spectrum.

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:34.440
BETH: Some employers do not recognise
the difficulties that these barriers

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.050
pose and may be unintentionally or
purposely restricting employment

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.339
opportunities for individuals with autism.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:46.120
Most of these barriers can be removed,
or reduced, by making 'reasonable

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.669
adjustments' when necessary.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.389
JOE: Barriers may start whilst
trying to find a suitable job.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.980
Search results may be confusing
and the information vague

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.470
especially through recruiters.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.870
This can create uncertainty as to
who is the employer, how much does

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.779
the job pay, what are the hours?

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:07.339
BETH: Filling in application forms may
cause problems with difficult questions

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:12.050
to answer about gaps in work history
and why they left a previous job, and

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.150
psychometric or personality tests.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:19.050
Questions about health or disability
may mean disclosing their autism

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.640
at the application stage which
may put employers off reading

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.430
their CV or offering an interview.

00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:29.140
Negative assumptions and limited
knowledge can stop an employer

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.690
processing the application.

00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:35.710
JOE: Some individuals are themselves put
off applying, due to negative experiences

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.960
of previous applications or interviews.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:42.329
Attending an interview can be really
daunting as they may find it hard

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.600
to know what to do, what to expect.

00:01:45.309 --> 00:01:48.979
They may have problems anticipating
questions and will be worried about the

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.110
process if they have not done it before.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.500
There may be other things involved
such group interviews, tests,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:00.069
activities or presentations,
these can all cause great concern.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.019
BETH: Eye contact and verbal and
non-verbal communication which

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.100
is often key in interviews may be
a problem, and how to respond to

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.550
‘question and answer’ sessions.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:14.120
Once the interview is over, they
may be unsure about how they did or

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.140
how it went or when they might hear.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.400
JOE: Success at the application and
interview stage may not alleviate

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:23.320
the issues of starting the job
and going through the process

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.200
of signing contracts and other
formalities can itself cause issues.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.650
Let alone other elements such as when
they start the job, the daily routine

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.660
and deadlines for projects, what do
they wear, how should they behave,

00:02:35.809 --> 00:02:39.040
when are their breaks, what are
their hours, holiday allowance, and

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.859
adjusting to the workplace environment.

